Playing the numbers game perfectly, many institutions recently have gained the status of high risers. For instance, the George Washington University, through the 2000s, was successful in lowering[ admission] rates from 49 to 33 per cent, built posh[ dorm]s and jacked its tuition. These measures led the college to be ranked 54 this year from being unranked.
