Prior to e-[commerce], before[ customers] had the[ myriad] of options they have today to consume products (via web portals, apps, social media, etc.),[ retailers] were able to differentiate themselves by the products inside their four[ walls]. The strategic practice of product differentiation became so prevalent and such a point of emphasis that it even gave way to the commonly heard par[lance] of[ retail] being a "merchant-led business."
